# S8-3d (QUALIFICATION, run 4 of 5): the AUDITS-OFF HANG SHAPES at four and at eight users, on c2-packed-tp4-8-diag-strace (c2-packed-tp4-8-time-gate
# plus the stall watch QWEN_FAST_STALL_DEADLINE_S=120, the stage log QWEN_FAST_SEQ_STAGE_LOG=1 (the handle log prints only through it), the allocator census QWEN_FAST_TRACE_CENSUS=1 with the graph off,
# the collectives handle log QWEN_FAST_CCL_HANDLE_LOG=1 and the handle guard in log mode QWEN_FAST_CCL_HANDLE_GUARD=log). Each run follows its own all-four reset. The shapes: concurrent4_steady, steady_resend and replay_concurrent4
# (the deterministic four-user factorial shapes: an engine build after many packed rounds, a rows=2 sequential replay), and their eight-user versions
# concurrent8_steady and replay_concurrent8, plus concurrent5_split (a lone user in block B beside a packed block A) and concurrent8_drain (live
# 8 to 1).
# WHY HERE: the audits-off hang was an eager collective reusing a handle a replayed trace baked. Two block traces on one shared model, sampler and
# collectives are a new exposure to exactly that, and the in-trace sampler fix is proven only at four users. The traffic-profile twin has no stall
# watch: a stall there waits for the job timeout and records nothing, so the hang shapes run on this diag twin.
# THERE IS NO QUALIFIED HANG FALLBACK AT 8 SEATS: the request-shard argmax arm has never run on hardware and the capture plug does not fit the
# eight-seat memory. A stall here means no production at eight seats until it is understood.
# READ: FIVE CONSECUTIVE COMPLETIONS (S8-3a to S8-3e), no stall-watch dump, every user at its budget, the handle-log and guard lines (a guard 'log'
# line names a handle reuse: read it before calling the run a pass), c2_smoke_check clean. One stall stops the window and the count restarts only on a
# new image or a recorded fix.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 10-30 min; the eight tests 15-25 min (a hang runs the ready loop, then the reset): 35 / 45 min.
# Stop rule: one stall stops the window (the handback still runs).
# SHIP WINDOW: the five-run count RESTARTS on the fix image: S8-3a to S8-3e are the five, in a row, each after its own reset. The earlier fix-on runs on
# the pre-ship image (three, on a subset of these shapes) do not count; a stall in any of the five stops the window and the count restarts only on a
# new image or a recorded fix.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-seats8 SHIP window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/seats8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's stop rule, its minutes and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8 is the SHIPPING image: the base SB8 builds
# from this branch with the eight-seat profile baked in as its serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and the platform session cap baked as its
# seat count (ENV THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP). Every job serves that one image, so the bytes that pass are the bytes that ship. Each job still
# names its profile explicitly, so none relies on the baked default. A commit that changes a file the image carries needs a new SB8 build and a
# new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8-diag-strace
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent4_steady,concurrent8_steady,steady_resend,replay_concurrent4,replay_concurrent8,concurrent5_split,concurrent8_drain
